{"availability":"available","full":"internette/workout-planner","name":"workout-planner","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-16T16:10:53Z","updated":"2026-10-16T00:23:23Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://workout-planner-one-lime.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://workout-planner-one-lime.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:55.391Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:55.391Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:55.391Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:42:54.797Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T20:52:30.067Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:55.391Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["\"Moonshot\" is a workout planner with a magical-girl theme. You schedule lifting and cycling sessions on a calendar, tick off exercises as you go, write a short diary entry about how it felt, and earn XP that moves you up a rank ladder. The interface comes from a Claude Design prototype, and everything is saved in Supabase."],"features":["Calendar: day, week and month views, with the current day highlighted and past sessions marked done or missed. A day can hold more than one workout: Day and Week views list each one, and a day counts as done (for its…","Workouts: lifting sessions (exercises with sets, reps, weight and rest) and cycling sessions (distance, elevation, duration, target effort). Both can repeat weekly for 12 weeks. Workout names are unique (ignoring case):…","Progress tracking: tick exercises off, mark rides complete, and enter what you actually rode against the plan.","Chronicle: a diary entry per session with mood, effort (1–5) and notes.","Spellbook (formerly the Spellbook): two views, switched with a toggle. Workouts lists every saved workout with its exercises and target areas; Exercises is your exercise library, grouped by workout, plus exercises not…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/internette/workout-planner/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"61d6bd7500e1d2da55c5ea51af2c558dd4a5513e37cead373ac923fededdf49b","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:55.490Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:55.490Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"\"Moonshot\" is a workout planner with a magical-girl theme. You schedule lifting and cycling sessions on a calendar, tick off exercises as you go, write a short diary entry about how it felt, and earn XP that moves you up a rank ladder. The interface comes from a Claude Design prototype, and everything is saved in Supabase.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/internette/workout-planner/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Screens inside a flow (an entry form, a workout editor) do not have addresses of their own yet; they keep the address of the nav item they were opened from. /arsenal, the Spellbook's old address, redirects to /spellbook. /welcome is the sign-in page and /design-system is the design-system site.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/internette/workout-planner/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"A sign-in provider that's off has no button on the front door, and /auth/login refuses it (and refuses a login with no provider named, which would otherwise show Auth0's page with every one).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/internette/workout-planner/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"Google needs an OAuth client from Google Cloud (Auth0's development keys work for testing); Apple needs a Services ID and key from a paid Apple Developer account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/internette/workout-planner/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"61d6bd7500e1d2da55c5ea51af2c558dd4a5513e37cead373ac923fededdf49b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/internette/workout-planner/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:55.491Z"},"o